easy
- add -p option to mkcd, mvcd, and cpcd
		- if specified this would create all necessary parent directories for your target to exist
- add directory history to o alias so it works more than once
- configure battery popup https://github.com/rjekker/i3-battery-popup/blob/master/i3-battery-popup
- configure bashhub (bash history on the cloud) https://github.com/rcaloras/bashhub-client

medium
- bfs early exit if not -f
- bfs -a to work more like find for simple cases
		- "bfsa rm *.swp" as less syntactically demanding "find -name *.swp -exec rm {} \;"
- keyboard shortcut to change kitty text size and reload all kitty terminals
- set up fzf/fdfind defaults
- look into kitty history preexec
